# ORWA ship / deploy

When the user says stage/commit/push/merge/ship/deploy, do the **full** path below. Do not stop at git push.

ORWA does **not** use Cloudflare or a separate CDN product. Frontends live on **WP Engine**; stale `index.html` is WP Engine **page cache** (`x-cacheable: SHORT`, `max-age=600`). Fix it with **wp-cli**, not CDN folklore.

## Git

- Small scoped commits only (`strapi: …`, `member-manager: …`).
- Leave unrelated work, screenshots (`tmp/`), `.playwright-mcp/`, and secret `.env` files unstaged. Write verification screenshots to `tmp/` (gitignored).
- `git fetch` → merge `origin/main` if needed → `git push origin <branch>` → merge/push to `main` as requested.

## Strapi (backend)

```bash
npx nx run strapi:docker-push
ssh root@admin.orwa.org "cd /var/opt/orwa-monorepo && docker compose pull strapi && docker compose up -d strapi"
```

- Compose file: `/var/opt/orwa-monorepo/docker-compose.yml`
- Container: `orwa-admin-v5`
- Smoke: wait for logs `Strapi started successfully`; hit `https://admin.orwa.org/admin` (200).

## Static frontends (WP Engine)

Apps under `sites/orwa/` on `orwa@orwa.ssh.wpengine.net`:

| App | Remote dir | Public URL |
|-----|------------|------------|
| member-manager | `member-manager/` | https://orwa.org/member-manager/ |
| conference-registration | `conference-registration/` | https://orwa.org/conference-registration/ |
| grant-map | `gapp-map/` | https://orwa.org/gapp-map/ |
| grant-application | `gapp-form/` | https://orwa.org/gapp-form/ |
| associate-directory | `associate-directory/` | https://orwa.org/associate-directory/ |
| awards | `awards-nomination-form/` | https://orwa.org/awards-nomination-form/ |
| scholarship-application | `scholarship-application/` | https://orwa.org/scholarship-application/ |

### Build (never `nx build` for production)

```bash
cd apps/<app>
# ALWAYS unset VITE_* first: OS env beats .env.production, and a shell that
# sourced another app's env (e.g. conference-registration's `…/api` endpoint)
# silently poisons this build.
env -u VITE_API_ENDPOINT -u VITE_API_KEY npx vite build --mode production
cat dist/assets/*.js | grep -c 'localhost:1337'              # must be 0
cat dist/assets/*.js | grep -c 'localhost:13370'             # must be 0
cat dist/assets/*.js | grep -o 'orwa.org/api/api' | wc -l    # must be 0 (doubled /api)
```

Endpoint convention differs per app — **member-manager** wants the host root
(`https://admin.orwa.org`, code appends `/api`); **conference-registration**,
**conference-hub**, `@orwa/terms-gate` want `https://admin.orwa.org/api`.
Mixing them up produces `/api/api/...` URLs (405 on login, 404 on `users/me`) —
shipped 2026-09-09. member-manager's `vite.config.ts` now refuses to build a
wrong endpoint; the grep above catches the other apps.

`nx build` can bake localhost from tracked `.env`. Vite `base: './'` required for subdirectory apps.

### Rsync (no `--delete`)

```bash
SSH=(ssh -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i "${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519")
rsync -avz --exclude '.DS_Store' --exclude 'package.json' \
  dist/ -e "${SSH[*]}" \
  orwa@orwa.ssh.wpengine.net:sites/orwa/<remote-dir>/
```

### REQUIRED — flush WP Engine caches (do this every frontend deploy)

`wp cache flush` = **object cache only**. It will **not** update live `index.html`.

```bash
ssh -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i "${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519" \
  orwa@orwa.ssh.wpengine.net 'wp page-cache flush && wp cdn-cache flush'
```

- `wp page-cache flush` — WP Engine page/Varnish cache (this is what kept serving old `index.html`)
- `wp cdn-cache flush` — WP Engine’s own edge-cache CLI (name is theirs; not an external CDN we run)

### Verify before declaring done

```bash
# Must show the NEW hashed bundle from this build (not the previous one)
curl -sS https://orwa.org/<app>/ | grep -oE 'index\.[a-f0-9]+\.js'
curl -sSI https://orwa.org/<app>/ | grep -iE 'x-cache|age:|last-modified'
```

If `x-cache: HIT` still shows the **old** hash after flush, re-run both flushes and re-check. Do not tell the user to “wait 10 minutes” or blame Cloudflare.

Also smoke in a headless browser (hard-reload / cache-disabled) — typecheck alone is not enough.

## Failure pattern (2026-09-09)

A deploy subagent built member-manager from a shell that had exported
conference-registration's `VITE_API_ENDPOINT=https://admin.orwa.org/api`.
The tracked `.env.production` was correct, but OS env won; the bundle carried
18 `admin.orwa.org/api/api/...` URLs and production login broke (405). The
review grep (`grep -oE 'https?://[^ ]+(/api)?'`) could not distinguish `/api`
from `/api/api`, so it passed. Grep for the literal `orwa.org/api/api`.

## Failure pattern (2026-08-12)

Shipping a member-manager fix while WP Engine still served prior `index.html` → browser kept loading `populate[payouts]=*` bundle → grant dashboard 400s. Origin was correct; **page cache** was not flushed. Always flush + verify hash.
